## H1 — Per-char OoStr concat (should be gone)

File: `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo`

Walker body (`c_sys_exec_last_arg`, L71–130):

- Linear index walk of joined C arg text; string-aware (`"..."` + `\\` skip); paren `depth` so nested commas do not split.
- Top-level `,` updates `last_start` to the first non-space after the comma (O(1) index, no copy).
- **One** extract after the walk: `let out = str_slice(args, last_start, n);`
- Source has **zero** `out = out + c` / `out = out + char_at` / `name = name + c` inside this function.
- Every `+` in the body is integer cursor/`depth` arithmetic (`i = i + 1`, `i + 1 < n`, …).
- Header comment (L121): “CRIT 7.2: one str_slice for the last arg span — no per-char OoStr thrash.”

Empty / degenerate:

| Case | Behavior | Heap |
|------|----------|------|
| `n == 0` | return literal `"oo_str_lit(\"\")"` | no scan |
| `last_start >= n` | `return args` | no extra slice |
| `str_slice` empty | `return args` | one empty slice then discard |

Emit mapping (`c_emit_ty.oo` L12–13): `str_slice` → `oo_str_slice`. `char_at` → `oo_char_at`. There is no `+` string concat in this fn, so lowered C **cannot** emit `oo_str_concat` for last-arg rebuild.

Lowered C of **this** compiler fn is not on disk this pass (`stage1_noarc.tmp.c` absent; host is the same 962960 B binary as 7.1). Honesty: H1 is source + deterministic lower, not a dumped `void c_sys_exec_last_arg`. Runtime primitive (`chs_rt_str.c` L197–212) is one `malloc` + `memcpy` of the UTF-8 span — **not** per-char concat.

Contrast (still OPEN elsewhere, not 7.2):

- `c_parse_secret_env` (`c_emit_secret.oo:60`) `name = name + c` — **7.10**
- `c_args_strip_cr` (`c_emit_args.oo:188`) `out = out + c` — CR strip on **sys_exec rest** (same file, same emit path; not last-arg extract)
- `c_emit_call_args` (`c_emit_call.oo:40`) `args = args + ", " + a` — join of the text this fn later scans

**H1: PASS.** The 7.2 concat leak is gone.

