## H2 — Long last-arg / many commas (heap vs time)

### Mechanism (code, not slogan)

`oo_char_at` (`ooda/runtime/chs_rt_str.c`):

- `utf8_byte_index` rescans from byte 0 to `idx` every call.
- Always `malloc`s a 1-char `OoStr`.

Loop `i in 0..n` with `char_at(args, i)` (plus a short space-skip `char_at` at each top-level comma) ⇒ **Θ(n²) time** + n short-lived 1-char strings.

`oo_str_slice(args, last_start, n)`:

- `end == n` → `be = s.len` (no second full `utf8_byte_index` for end).
- Still `oo_chars_len(args)` once (O(n)) + one `utf8_byte_index` for `last_start` + **one** heap copy of the last span.

Call-in (`c_emit_secret_guard.oo` L130–140): `sys_exec` sink → `last = c_sys_exec_last_arg(args)` → if `c_arg_is_cap_ident(last)` then alias-resolved refuse. Adjacent emit (`c_emit_lower.oo` L156–162) uses `c_args_drop_first` (already **one** `str_slice`) + **`c_args_strip_cr` twice** (still per-char concat of `rest`). Do not attribute strip_cr thrash to 7.2.

### Measurements (cheap emit-c of generated fixtures)

Harness: ephemeral `/tmp/s72_mem_1084524/` (not landed). `oodac emit-c` of:

- **last_N** — `sys_exec(sys, "sh", "-c", "x"*N)` (hits last-arg walk + **one** slice of the huge last span)
- **strcommas_N** — last arg is N commas inside `"..."` (string-aware: must **not** update `last_start` per comma)
- **commas_N** — N extra `"a"` argv slots then last `"Z"` (many top-level commas; last span tiny)
- **println_N** — `println("x"*N)` control (no last-arg / no strip_cr)

Isolated retimes (`/usr/bin/time` `%e` sec / `%M` maxrss KB; 1 trial):

| N | last src B | last sec | last RSS KB | strcommas sec | strcommas RSS | println sec | println RSS | commas sec | commas RSS |
|---|-----------:|---------:|------------:|--------------:|--------------:|------------:|------------:|-----------:|-----------:|
| 200 | 289 | 0.04 | 5424 | 0.04 | 5560 | 0.03 | 4792 | 0.43 | 17852 |
| 400 | 489 | 0.07 | 5816 | 0.07 | 5952 | 0.05 | 5176 | 1.34 | 31164 |
| 800 | 889 | 0.19 | 6968 | 0.15 | 6968 | 0.20 | 5944 | 4.95 | 60728 |
| 1600 | 1689 | 0.45 | 8632 | 0.79 | 8632 | 0.27 | 7480 | 27.33 | 128696 |
| 4096 | 4185 | 1.44 | 14392 | — | — | 1.54 | 11976 | — | — |
| 8192 | 8281 | 7.06 | 23736 | — | — | 5.71 | 19516 | — | — |

Product fixtures (same binary):

| Fixture | src B | sec | maxrss KB | rc | note |
|---------|------:|----:|----------:|---:|------|
| `secret_sys_exec_pass.oo` | 194 | 0.07 | 5944 | 0 | last is string lit |
| `secret_sys_exec_fail.oo` | 188 | 0.02 | 4792 | 1 | last is SECRET IDENT |
| `secret_sys_exec_argv_pass.oo` | 214 | 0.06 | 5944 | 0 | clean extra argv |
| `secret_sys_exec_argv_fail.oo` | 232 | 0.05 | 4792 | 1 | SECRET mid-argv (walker, not last) |
| `hello.oo` | 583 | 0.09 | 6896 | 0 | no sys_exec |
| tiny `println(1)` | 34 | 0.05 | 4336 | 0 | control |

**Read of the numbers:**

1. **last_N RSS** 5.4 → 5.8 → 7.0 → 8.6 → 14.4 → 23.7 MB. Linear in source size. **Not** a quadratic concat buffer on the last span.
2. **strcommas_N RSS matches last_N** at 200–1600. In-string commas do not allocate per comma; `last_start` stays at the last top-level span.
3. **println_N** is ~2–4 MB leaner than last_N at the same N. The delta is sys_exec emit (`strip_cr` + last-arg walk + one slice + argv C text), not n² last-arg rebuild.
4. **Time** 4096→8192 is ~4.9× (last) / ~3.7× (println) for 2× source. Superlinear, consistent with `char_at` + lex. last vs println at 8192 is **+1.35 s / +4 MB** — strip_cr + extra walk, **not** a second n² concat bomb (that would dwarf println).
5. **commas_N** RSS ≈ 80 KB · N and time 0.43 → 27 s is **token list + `c_emit_call_args` join + strip_cr**, not last-arg extract (last span is `"Z"`). Do not attribute that curve to 7.2.

**H2 heap: PASS.** **H2 time: residual** (same class as 7.1 / lex; 8 KiB last arg finishes; 64 KiB rail would be slow, not a new 7.2 leak).

