## Close bar for 7.2 (memory)

Path-A **may close 7.2 as memory-floor PASS** if process accepts:

1. Concat gone (proven here).
2. Slice ≡ the alpha “buffer” (proven here; matches `t1_memory.oot` M-SG3 / 7.1 H3).
3. `char_at` quadratic **time** stays a named residual (compiler-wide), not a 7.2 reopen.
4. `c_args_strip_cr` per-char rebuild stays a **named adjacent** leak — do not silently fold it into 7.2 FIXED.

Re-open 7.2 only if concat returns inside `c_sys_exec_last_arg`, or emit-c of ≤64 KiB **last** arg **OOMs** / RSS grows as Θ(n²) **from the last-arg extract** (not from strip_cr / token list).

